  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "The taxi fare in Gotham City is \\(\\$2.40\\) for the first \\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\) mile and additional mileage charged at the rate \\(\\$0.20\\) for each additional \\(0.1\\) mile. You plan to give the driver a \\(\\$2\\) tip. How many miles can you ride for \\(\\$10\\)?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3.0\\)",
    "B": "\\(3.25\\)",
    "C": "\\(3.3\\)",
    "D": "\\(3.5\\)",
    "E": "\\(3.75\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First set aside the \\(\\$2\\) tip and the \\(\\$2.40\\) fare covering the first \\(0.5\\) mile. This leaves\n\\[\n\\$10-\\$2-\\$2.40=\\$5.60\n\\]\nfor additional mileage. Each additional \\(0.1\\) mile costs \\(\\$0.20\\), so the remaining money buys \\(5.60\\div0.20=28\\) such portions.\n\nThe greatest distance is therefore\n\\[\n0.5+28(0.1)=3.3\\text{ miles},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
